<domain>
## Phase Boundary

Confirm that the layered merge on `recon/tui-interaction-consistency-2026-09-07`
— origin's 12-phase GSD milestone (`b9a8876`) adopted as base, plus 9 commits
porting local's independent line's unique subsystems (`985f602`) on top — is
architecturally sound, not just green on `make validate`/`make test`. This is
a verification phase over already-executed reconciliation work, not new
feature development. Wiring `install_actions.py`/`agent_policy.py` into the
UI is explicitly out of scope here (Phase 12.2). Container e2e is out of
scope here (Phase 12.3) — this phase is static/manual-smoke verification only.

</domain>

<decisions>
## Implementation Decisions

### Verification depth
- **D-01:** Static/automated checks (import graph, orphaned modules, vulture,
  coverage) PLUS a manual smoke walkthrough of the TUI in `tmux` (navigation
  across Catalog/Doctor/Uninstall/Policies views) — no real install/uninstall
  actions executed yet, that's Phase 12.3's job.

### Tier remapping audit
- **D-02:** Full individual audit of all 11 re-added registry rows (`glab`,
  `drawio-desktop`, `drawio-cli`, `pi`, `ponytail`, `openspec`, `superpowers`,
  `softaworks-agent-toolkit`, `matt-pocock-skills`, `opengsd`, `spec-kit`)
  against origin's real tier semantics (system = machine prerequisite, user =
  personal-pick tool, ai = agent-facing tooling) — not just trusting the
  porting agent's skill-pack/agent→`ai`, everything-else→`user` heuristic.
  Correct any row found misclassified.

### Pre-existing failing test
- **D-03:** Fix `tests/test_version_status.py::test_fresh_manager_snapshot_issues_zero_queries`
  within this phase, even though it was confirmed failing identically on
  unmodified origin `b9a8876` (not introduced by the reconciliation) —
  keeps the branch fully green before Phase 12.3's container e2e run, so a
  future failure there is unambiguously new.

### Ported-but-unwired code hygiene
- **D-04:** Verify `installer/install_actions.py` and `installer/agent_policy.py`
  don't break `make validate` (vulture dead-code, import correctness,
  coverage floor) as inert-but-valid modules — do NOT wire them into the UI
  or add integration tests here. That wiring decision belongs to Phase 12.2.

### Claude's Discretion
- Exact static-analysis tooling/commands beyond what `make validate` already
  runs (e.g., whether a dedicated import-graph check is needed on top of
  vulture) — planner's call based on what `make validate`'s existing gates
  already cover.
- Whether fixing D-03's test requires touching `installer/version_status.py`
  logic or only the test's fixture/mock setup — research/implementation-time
  call, informed by reading the actual failure.

</decisions>

