<objective>
Verify — not merely re-run `make validate`/`make test` on — the layered merge of origin's
12-phase GSD milestone (`b9a8876`, adopted as base) with local's independent line's unique
subsystems (`985f602`, ported on top via commits `8416d5c`..`a570bf3` on
`recon/tui-interaction-consistency-2026-09-07`) is architecturally sound. This phase has no
`REQUIREMENTS.md` entries (ROADMAP lists this inserted phase's Requirements as `TBD`); its four
locked decisions in `12.1-CONTEXT.md` (D-01 verification depth, D-02 tier remapping audit, D-03
pre-existing failing test, D-04 ported-but-unwired code hygiene) are this plan's concrete,
testable requirements and are cited as `D-01`..`D-04` throughout.

Three closed findings drive this plan's three tasks, each already confirmed live on this
machine on 2026-09-10 before writing this plan (not assumed):

1. **D-03**: `tests/test_version_status.py::test_fresh_manager_snapshot_issues_zero_queries` is
   the ONLY failing test in the entire suite (confirmed via a full `uv run pytest -q` run with
   and without `--deselect` on that one test). Root cause: this machine's real `PNPM_HOME` env
   var leaks into `installer/ownership.py::owner_dirs`'s unconditional `os.environ.get` read,
   which the test's `_which_for_fixture`/`_node_tool` fixtures never isolate — unlike
   `tests/test_ownership.py`, which already does via `monkeypatch.setenv`/`delenv`. This
   reproduces identically on unmodified origin `b9a8876` per D-03, confirming it predates the
   reconciliation.
2. **D-02**: all 11 registry rows commit `9f6274b` re-added were individually audited against
   origin's real tier semantics and this registry's own established precedents (`gh`↔`glab`,
   `mmdc`↔`drawio-cli`/`drawio-desktop`, `claude`/`codex`/`opencode`/`cursor-agent`/`antigravity`
   ↔`pi`, `codegraph`/`graphify`/`rtk`↔the seven `skill_pack` rows). No misclassification found.
3. **D-04**: a direct import-graph grep (`grep -rnE ... setup.py installer/wizard_app.py
   installer/app.py installer/catalog_tui.py installer/engine.py installer/ui_common.py`,
   0 matches) plus a live tmux Policies-view capture (only 9 policies render; no
   agent-environment/permission-audit row) confirm `installer/install_actions.py` and
   `installer/agent_policy.py` (and their sibling modules) are genuinely orphaned from the live
   app — exactly `.claude/architecture.md` rule 5's "only its own test keeping it covered"
   definition of an orphan helper. Locked D-04 explicitly declines wiring or even a TODO note
   here (Phase 12.2 owns that decision) — this plan verifies without blocking, per that decision.

Purpose: close the phase's verification scope (D-01: static/automated checks PLUS a manual
tmux smoke walkthrough, no real install/uninstall — that stays Phase 12.3's job) so the branch
is provably, not just apparently, ready for Phase 12.3's container e2e run.

Output: a fully green test suite (zero known failures); a permanent, individually-reasoned
regression test pinning D-02's tier audit; a recorded static import-graph audit confirming
D-04's orphan finding without new wiring; and a recorded, verbatim real-terminal tmux
transcript proving all six views render correctly with zero real-machine mutation.
</objective>

