<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| CI/dev-machine environment variables (`PNPM_HOME`, `UV_TOOL_BIN_DIR`) → unit test assertions | A test previously let real host environment state leak into a deterministic assertion (`installer/ownership.py::owner_dirs` reads `os.environ` unconditionally), producing a host-dependent pass/fail rather than a reproducible one |
| Task 3's temporary verification script → the real `uv run setup.py` process in a real terminal | Drives the actual production entry point through `tmux send-keys`; must never reach a key that mutates this machine's real shell rc files or performs a real install/uninstall |
| Ported-but-unwired local subsystems (`install_actions.py`'s multi-hook `post_install`, `agent_policy.py`'s permission auditing) → production composition root (`setup.py`) | Real subprocess/file-write-capable code currently has zero live callers into the app a user actually runs — confirmed inert, not reachable from any real user action, pending Phase 12.2's wiring decision |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Severity | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-12.1-01 | Tampering | `tests/test_version_status.py::test_fresh_manager_snapshot_issues_zero_queries` | low | mitigate | Task 1 pins `PNPM_HOME`/`UV_TOOL_BIN_DIR` via `monkeypatch.delenv` so the test's ownership-attribution assertion is deterministic regardless of the host machine's real pnpm/uv install location (D-03). |
| T-12.1-02 | Elevation of Privilege | `installer/install_actions.py` / `installer/agent_policy.py` — ported, unwired subsystems with real subprocess/file-write capability | medium | accept | Task 3 confirms zero production callers into `setup.py`'s composition root via a static import-graph check plus a live Policies-view smoke capture; intentionally left unwired per locked CONTEXT.md D-04 — Phase 12.2 owns the wiring decision, this phase only verifies the gap is real and bounded. |
| T-12.1-03 | Tampering | Task 3's `verify-static-and-smoke.sh` tmux session driving the real `uv run setup.py` process | low | mitigate | The script is navigation-only (keys `1`-`6` then `q`, never `space`/`enter`); `--link-mode centralized` skips the one interactive prompt that could reach a write path; a before/after `stat` mtime check on `~/.myshellrc`/`~/.zshrc` is the script's own automated proof of zero mutation, matching ONESHOT-RULES.md Rule 5 — already verified live on this exact machine (2026-09-10, mtimes unchanged) before this plan was written. |

</threat_model>

